# Declare a Model card

## Prerequisites

- py-wyrd installed and `WYRD_SERVER_URL` set
- A running server

## Recipe

```python
from wyrd.model import ModelCard

# 1. Build the card
card = ModelCard(
    name="churn-classifier",
    version="1.0.0",
    spec={
        "provider": "openai",
        "model_id": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "input_schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"text": {"type": "string"}}},
        "output_schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"label": {"type": "string"}}},
    },
)

# 2. Optionally save locally
card.save()

# 3. Register
import wyrd
wyrd.cards.register(card)
```

## Add a data dependency

Reference the training dataset by CardRef so the registry can derive lineage:

```python
from wyrd.spec import CardRef

card = ModelCard(
    name="churn-classifier",
    version="1.0.0",
    spec={
        "provider": "openai",
        "model_id": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "training_data": CardRef(name="churn-dataset", version="0.3.0").to_dict(),
    },
)
```

## Notes

- Keep `name` stable across versions.
- Put operational rules (rate limits, cost, latency SLA) in the spec rather
  than in free-form annotations.

